From 2f1fd810180cfe8bbacac60810d5098459cd0dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:07:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] hw/display/pvg: private textures stay on the GPU;
 optional dirty-tracked upload cache

- MTLStorageModePrivate render targets are not written back and not
  re-uploaded: the host image is resident, guest memory is marked stale and
  flushed when something reads it from the guest side (SynchronizeResources,
  Unmap, uploads of an overlapping image, CPU-side blits / mipmaps, an image
  about to be re-created for another level). ~200-280 MiB per 500 command
  buffers not copied; executor time per 500 cmdbufs ~680-1100 -> ~500 ms.
  Property private-resident (default on).
- upload-cache (default off): KVM dirty logging on guest RAM keeps textures on
  the GPU while their pages stay clean. Works, but guest pages are almost all
  physically scattered (one run per page) and entries churn, so tracking costs
  about what it saves; kept for experiments.
- physmem: physical_memory_range_is_dirty() (no clear, no KVM call).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
